@obverse 
1. _3(iku) GAN2 a-sza3_ i-na _a-gar3_ nam-zu-um{ki} 
#tr.ts: šalašat ikû eqlum ina ugārim namzum
#tr.en: A field of 300 SAR in the Namzum irrigation district

2. i-ta {d}utu-la-ma-si2 nin-ma-an-szum2 
#tr.ts: itā šamaš-lama(s)sī nin-manšum
#tr.en: next to (the field of) Šamaš-lamassī (and) Nin-manšum

3. u3 i-ta um-mi-{d}{i7}idigna 
#tr.ts: u itā ummī-idiqlat
#tr.en: and next to (the field of) Ummī-idiqlat;

4. _3(iku) GAN2 4(u) sar <a-sza3>_ i-na _a-gar3_ nam-zu-um{ki} 
#tr.ts: šalašat ikû erbâ mūšar eqlum ina ugārim namzum
#tr.en: a field of 340 SAR in the Namzum irrigation district

5. i-ta mu-na-wi-ir-tum 
#tr.ts: itā muna(w)wirtum
#tr.en: next to (the field of) Munawwirtum;

6. _1(esze3) 1(iku) GAN2 a-sza3_ i-na _a-gar3_ ma-ha!-na 
#tr.ts: ištēn ebel ištēn ikû eqlum ina ugārim maḫana 
#tr.en: a field of 700 SAR in the Maḫana irrigation district;

7. _1(disz) sar e2_ i-na _ga2-gi-a{ki}_ 
#tr.ts: ištēn mūšar bītum ina gagîm
#tr.en: a house of 1 SAR in the cloister

8. _da e2_ la-ma-sa3-tum  
#tr.ts: ṭēḫi bīt lama(s)satum
#tr.en: adjacent to the house of Lamassatum;

9. _1(disz) sag-geme2_ {d}utu-la-ma-si2 
#tr.ts: ištēt amtum šamaš-lama(s)sī
#tr.en: one female slave (named) Šamaš-lamassī;

10. bu-szu-sza wa-ar-ka-sa3 
#tr.ts: būšûša warka(s)sa
#tr.en: her inherited property (and) her personal possessions,

11. isz-tu pe2-e a-di _ku3-sig17_-ma? sza 
#tr.ts: ištu pê adi ḫurāṣimma ša
#tr.en: everything (lit. from chaff to gold) is what

12. {disz}mu-na-wi-ir-tum _lukur {d}utu dumu-munus_ {d}nanna-ma-an-szum2 
#tr.ts: muna(w)wirtum nadīt šamaš mārat nanna-manšum
#tr.en: Munawwirtum nadītu of Šamaš daughter of Nanna-manšum

13. a-na sig-i3-li2-sza! _dumu-munus_ GABA-dingir-ra  
#tr.ts: ana ipqu-ilīša mārat gaba-dingira
#tr.en: to Ipqu-ilīša daughter of Gaba-dingira

14. ma-ri-sza id-di-nu 
#tr.ts: mārīša iddinu
#tr.en: her child has given.

15. a-di mu-na-wi-ir-<tum> ba-al-t,a3-[at] 
#tr.ts: adi muna(w)wirtum balṭat
#tr.en: As long as Munawwirtum lives

16. _a-sza3# e2 geme2_ qa2-sa3-ma u2-ka#-[al] 
#tr.ts: eqlam bītam amtam qā(s)sāma ukāl
#tr.en: will have the usufruct of (lit. her hand will hold) field, house (and) slave.

17. [isz]-tu i-lu-sza iq-te-ru-[szi] 
#tr.ts: ištu ilūša iqterūši
#tr.en: When she will die (lit. her god will summon her)

@reverse  
1. sza [sig]-i3-li2-sza#-ma 
#tr.ts: ša ipqu-ilīšāma
